#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:6
msgid "Derive Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:8
msgid ""
"**Derive procedural macros** are decorated with the "
"`#[proc_macro_derive(TraitName)]` attribute. They take in the token stream "
"of a type definition and return a token stream containing additional "
"implementations:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:17
msgid "// Parse the struct/enum item, generate `MyDebug` implementation...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:22
msgid ""
"**Additive Output:** The returned token stream is compiled alongside the "
"type definition in the same scope. It does not replace the type definition "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:24
msgid ""
"**Helper Attributes:** Derive macros can declare optional helper attributes "
"that can be used on struct fields or enum variants, configured in the derive "
"declaration: `#[proc_macro_derive(MyTrait, attributes(my_helper))]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:31
msgid ""
"The `item` TokenStream represents the entire struct, enum, or union "
"definition, including its attributes, generic parameters, braces, and fields."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:33
msgid ""
"Discuss helper attributes: helper attributes are matched by the derive macro "
"to let users customize the code generation (e.g., `#[my_helper(rename = "
"\"field\")]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/derive.md:36
msgid ""
"Note that the argument to `proc_macro_derive` dictates how this derive macro "
"is imported and triggered, but does not actually constrain which items it "
"generates `impl` blocks for. Some derive macros may impl multiple traits (as "
"does `thiserror::Error`, for example); derive macros must be well behaved "
"and document their effects."
msgstr ""
